{
  "reviewer": "claim_evidence_auditor",
  "paper_id": "bicycle-infrastructure-paper",
  "run_status": "ok",
  "summary": "The 18-page paper is a short pilot on LLM extraction of bicycle-infrastructure openings from Norwegian news, plus a housing-listing appendix. I found 17 claim-evidence problems. The main ones are:\n- Units change between articles, hits and openings in the pilot funnel (Section 3.1.2 and Figure 1).\n- The 97 percent human–LLM agreement and the 'same date for all three' result rest on 3 relevant articles covering 2 openings. The abstract and introduction do not carry the caveat that Section 4 gives.\n- Full-run counts (92 articles, 43 projects, 29 dated) are presented as pipeline outputs, but no precision or date check was done on the full run.\n- Location and municipality extraction is claimed but not validated.\n- Section 5 seasonal and county statements have no supporting display.\n- Footnote 3 says both human coders coded the Stord article as not relevant, which contradicts Table 3 and Section 4.1.\n- Several generalisations go beyond one case or a few cases: the NVDB claim, 'scalable', and 'keyword search alone is too noisy'.\n- Two housing-listing category labels ('Proximity', and a 'first type in the table' rule contradicted by the bysykkelstativ example) are broader than what they measure.\nHousing-listing shares (Table 8, Figures 2–4) and the Table 6 totals reconcile with the text. External literature claims could not be checked against retained artifacts.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "CEA-001",
      "category": "unit_mismatch",
      "finding_summary": "The pilot funnel text and Figure 1 caption report '2 of 34 unique articles' and '2 of 70 search hits' as concerning an opening that took place, but the 2 is a count of distinct openings, while Section 3.1.4 reports five articles coded relevant for those two openings.",
      "issue_type": "manuscript_issue",
      "severity": "medium",
      "confidence": "high",
      "location": {
        "page": 4,
        "page_label": "4",
        "section": "3.1.2 Pilot sample / Figure 1",
        "text_quote": "Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place.",
        "precision": "exact"
      },
      "claim_text": "Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place; Figure 1 caption: Only 2 of 70 search hits concern a cycling infrastructure opening that actually took place.",
      "assessment": "no",
      "cannot_verify_reason": null,
      "evidence_summary": "Figure 1's bars switch unit from hits (70) to articles (34, 5) to 'Distinct openings that took place' (2). Section 3.1.4 says 'Of the five relevant articles, only two unique openings were found. Four of the articles mention Homborsund and one Stod.' Articles about the two openings therefore number five (three after the validation recoding), not two. The 6 percent is 2/34, which divides openings by articles. The abstract's 'contained only two actual openings' is correctly worded, but the body sentence and caption are not.",
      "source_objects": [
        {
          "id": "S1",
          "type": "text",
          "label": "page 4 text (Section 3.1.2)",
          "path": "work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_004.md",
          "page": 4,
          "page_label": "4",
          "section": "3.1.2",
          "text_quote": "Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place.",
          "url": null,
          "object_id": "OBJ-1a119a3cb70f2153fc56dd97",
          "correspondence": "text",
          "verification_note": "Figure 1 chart viewed on page_004.png: bars 70, 34 (49 % retained), 5 (15 % retained), 2 'Distinct openings that took place'."
        },
        {
          "id": "S2",
          "type": "text",
          "label": "page 5 text (Section 3.1.4)",
          "path": "work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_005.md",
          "page": 5,
          "page_label": "5",
          "section": "3.1.4",
          "text_quote": "Of the five relevant articles, only two unique openings were found.",
          "url": null,
          "object_id": "OBJ-9d16c139938370d7a97e77c6",
          "correspondence": "text",
          "verification_note": "Five relevant articles, four on Homborsund and one on Stod."
        }
      ],
      "claim_evidence_links": [
        {
          "claim_text": "Only 2 of the 34 unique articles concern an opening that took place",
          "source_object_ids": [
            "S1",
            "S2"
          ],
          "relation": "contradicts",
          "note": "Five articles were coded relevant and concern the two openings; 2 counts openings."
        }
      ],
      "numeric_check": null,
      "suggested_fix": "Keep one unit per statement. Report articles coded relevant (5, or 3 after the validation recoding) and distinct openings (2) separately. Restate the 6 percent and the 'Only 2 of 70 search hits' caption accordingly."
    },
