        "precision": "exact"
      },
      "claim_text": "Of the 44 projects, 18 have an article reporting an official opening ceremony. Of these, 17 can be dated to the day, compared with 2 of the 26 projects without a reported ceremony. This suggests that the precision of the dates is not random but depends on how much attention an opening receives.",
      "assessment": "partially",
      "cannot_verify_reason": null,
      "evidence_summary": "The counts are internally consistent with Table 6 (17+2=19 projects dated to the day) and with the 44 denominator, but the ceremony cross-tabulation is not displayed. A reported ceremony is a measure of coverage, and an article describing a ceremony naturally states a specific date, so the pattern is partly mechanical. The authors treat it as a hypothesis ('suggests'), and model (1) is a proposed test. The 44 projects include the Stord project, which humans did not all code as an opening (see CEA-009).",
