        "text_quote": "showing that keyword search alone is too noisy and that an LLM filter is needed.",
        "precision": "exact"
      },
      "claim_text": "A pilot of 70 search hits, of which 34 were unique articles, contained only two actual openings, showing that keyword search alone is too noisy and that an LLM filter is needed.",
      "assessment": "partially",
      "cannot_verify_reason": null,
      "evidence_summary": "The pilot used the single term 'sykkelvei' (Section 3.1.1), which the paper says returns about 13 800 hits in three years versus about 530 for 'åpning sykkelvei'. Only the broad term was evaluated, so the pilot shows that this broad term is noisy: 5 of 34 unique articles were coded relevant. It does not show that no keyword or rule-based filter would suffice, nor that an LLM filter's precision is adequate (see CEA-006). The paper's later wording, 'The low yield points to the need for an LLM to filter', is softer than the abstract's.",
